<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan de Grijalva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1490–<a href="/years/1527">1527</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan de Grijalva was a Spanish conquistador who led the second expedition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> to the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1518. He sailed past Cozumel, fought at Champotón and followed the Gulf coast to the river now named after him, gathering the first reports of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>. His voyage prepared the way for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a>. He was killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a> in 1527.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-de-grijalva.jpg" alt="Juan de Grijalva" width="320" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_de_Grijalva.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
